{"qid":"Q2267508","names":["Trịnh lords"],"title":"Trịnh lords","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Trịnh lords (chúa Trịnh) were a military clan that seized effective control of the Lê imperial court in Hanoi from 1572 onward, ruling the northern polity of Đàng Ngoài while the Lê emperors served as figureheads. Their long rivalry with the southern Nguyễn lords produced a partition across the Gianh River, formalized by intermittent warfare between 1627 and 1672 and then a long stalemate. Trịnh Tráng (r. 1623–1652) and his successors maintained a sophisticated bureaucratic and military apparatus, but the dynasty's authority collapsed rapidly in 1786–1788 when the Tây Sơn movement swept north, deposed the last Trịnh lord Trịnh Bồng, and reunified Vietnam under a new order.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The general extent of Trịnh control over northern Vietnam is well documented, but exact border shifts during the Trịnh–Nguyễn Wars are not always mapped with precision in secondary literature.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Trịnh lords","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tr%E1%BB%8Bnh_lords"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Lê–Mạc War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%AA%E2%80%93M%E1%BA%A1c_War"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Đàng Ngoài","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C4%90%C3%A0ng_Ngo%C3%A0i"}],"britannica":"topic/Trinh-family","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Trịnh lords","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Trịnh Kiểm","nativeName":"鄭檢","roman":"Trịnh Kiểm","start":1545,"end":1570,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Trịnh Cối","nativeName":"鄭榙","roman":"Trịnh Cối","start"